jake: small wording nit — "automatic fallback to smaller model variant" should be "fallback to compatible model variant (lower-cost or quantized)" — avoids implying we always pick smaller token-limit models. also add a one-line example showing the user-facing behavior: `if response.status == 429 -> try model: 'openai-micro-quant-v1'`

aline: i drafted a compact SDK snippet for retries + fallback. feel free to paste it into the PR under "Client best practices". shows exponential backoff + honoring `Retry-After` and a cold-start max attempt.

aline: ```js
// JS SDK - robust retry + fallback
async function generateWithFallback(client, opts) {
  const maxAttempts = 5;
  let attempt = 0;
  let model = opts.model || 'redwood-standard-v1';
  while (attempt < maxAttempts) {
    try {
      return await client.generate({ ...opts, model });
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.status === 429) {
        const retryAfter = parseInt(err.headers?.['retry-after'] || '1', 10);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, Math.min(2 ** attempt * 500, 5000) + retryAfter * 1000));
        // on repeated 429s, switch to a compatible fallback model
        if (attempt >= 2) model = 'redwood-compact-quant-v1';
        attempt++;
        continue;
      }
      if (err.code === 'CONTEXT_WINDOW_EXCEEDED') {
        throw new Error('Context length too large — recommend truncating or using streaming/KV cache');
      }
      throw err;
    }
  }
  throw new Error('Retries exhausted');
}
```

maria.k: perfect — can you also add the brief migration snippet for python users who relied on auto-trimming behavior? we need a clear callout: "old clients silently trimmed context -> new clients should check for CONTEXT_WINDOW_EXCEEDED and surface to users or fallback to cached prompts."

jake: +1. suggest a single-line red warning block in the docs: "If you see CONTEXT_WINDOW_EXCEEDED, avoid silent truncation — prefer explicit truncation or KV cache to preserve user intent."

